# SemText npl-thought — typed associative thought bubble, all display modes
# Direction A "Slate Console" (house convention). Six example panels in one
# frame, one per display mode the tag provides: the enhanced canonical
# classified set, the enhanced unknown-type warning, the enhanced no-type
# sub-container, the enhanced class-form spelling, the enhanced light-theme
# set, and the JS-off degraded form. The invariant the design must broadcast:
# a thought is a QUIET margin note — an accent rule, a faint tint and a
# small-caps type label — with its text always fully legible. The LABEL is
# the non-colour cue: every type is told apart by its word, never by hue
# alone. npl-thought never occludes or hides the authored text (occlusion
# belongs to the sem-spoiler / quiz tier).
#
# MODE 1 — enhanced, canonical classified thought:
#   visible: a stack of per-thought note cards, each with a left accent rule
#     (soft violet), a faint violet tint (never opaque), squared-left /
#     rounded-right corners; each card is led by a tiny small-caps single-word
#     type label (muted slate) above one near-white bar of body text.
#   must never: fill a card opaque; differ in anatomy from card to card;
#     rely on colour alone to tell the types apart.
# MODE 2 — enhanced, unknown type (warning):
#   visible: one normal labelled card, then a second card whose left rule is
#     DASHED in amber with a faint amber tint, and whose label reads the value
#     plus an "unknown" suffix (amber-tinted) — "BALLOON · UNKNOWN".
#   must never: hide or drop the unknown child; render it as structure; use a
#     solid (non-dashed) rule; signal the warning by colour alone (the word
#     "unknown" must be present).
# MODE 3 — enhanced, no-type sub-container:
#   visible: one labelled accent card, then its nested prose lines with NO
#     card chrome — no rule, no tint, no label — set slightly indented; the
#     sub-container applies nothing to itself, only its typed children carry
#     chrome.
#   must never: give the un-typed lines a card, a rule, a tint, or a label;
#     change the typed card's anatomy.
# MODE 4 — enhanced, class-form (data-type):
#   visible: a single labelled accent card, identical in anatomy to mode 1's
#     cards, driven by the authored data-type spelling.
#   must never: look different from the element-form card.
# MODE 5 — enhanced, light theme:
#   visible: the same two-card labelled stack on a light surface — near-white
#     card, slate text, blue accent rule — every label and body bar meeting AA
#     contrast against its card.
#   must never: show dark-mode cards on a light panel; drop the accent rule;
#     dim the label below legibility.
# MODE 6 — JS-off degraded:
#   visible: plain authored prose only — short placeholder bars as ordinary
#     unstyled lines, no cards, no rules, no tints, no labels.
#   must never: show a card, an accent rule, a tint, or a generated small-caps
#     label when the script has not run; hide any authored line.
#
# The type label is the one place real characters appear — one short
# uppercase/small-caps word per typed child (OBSERVATION, QUESTION, RELATION,
# CONCERN, AFFIRMATION, BALLOON · UNKNOWN). Everywhere else the mock uses
# abstract placeholder bars, never letters, digits, or sentences.
#
# Reference renders: the site's /reference/npl-thought/ page is source-view
# only today, so the enhanced form is judged from a throwaway fixture captured
# with the room's headless Chrome (fixture HTML + current
# themes/_vocabulary.css + the built npl.js). The `npl-thought-render-*`
# references below are those fixture captures; `npl-thought-fullpage-1280.png`
# is the site page (source view + chrome) from `npm run snap:tag -- npl-thought`.
schema: '0.4'
id: reference-npl-thought
type: image
quality: high
service: gemini
model: gemini-2.5-flash-image

prompt:
  text: |
    Dark-mode UI mockup of six reference-page panels in a three-by-two grid
    illustrating one typed thought-bubble element in its six display modes,
    wide 16:9, flat technical illustration (screenshot-like, not 3D). Dark
    slate navy background (#0F172A) with a barely visible thin grid and a
    faint violet radial glow upper-left. Six equal panels sit in three
    columns and two rows, separated by thin slate hairline dividers, each
    panel a dark slate card (#1E293B) with a thin slate hairline border,
    squared corners, deep soft shadow; a small dim caption bar sits above
    each panel.

    TOP-LEFT panel — ENHANCED CANONICAL. Three stacked note cards, each
    indented from the panel's left, with a thin 3px violet left rule, a
    barely-there violet tint over the card (NOT a solid fill), and
    squared-left / softly rounded-right corners. Each card is led by one
    short small-caps single-word label bar in muted slate (read it as a
    type word), above one wider near-white bar of body text. The three cards
    share one identical anatomy.

    TOP-MIDDLE panel — ENHANCED UNKNOWN TYPE. Two stacked cards: the first a
    normal violet-ruled labelled card; the second with a DASHED left rule in
    amber and a faint amber tint, its label in amber-tinted small caps and
    noticeably longer (a value word followed by an "unknown" suffix). Both
    cards keep near-white body bars.

    TOP-RIGHT panel — ENHANCED NO-TYPE SUB-CONTAINER. One violet-ruled
    labelled card, then two plain unlabelled near-white prose bars beneath it
    with NO rule, NO tint and NO label — set very slightly indented. The
    un-typed lines carry no card chrome at all.

    BOTTOM-LEFT panel — ENHANCED CLASS-FORM. One violet-ruled labelled card
    alone in generous empty space — pixel-comparable in anatomy to the
    top-left cards.

    BOTTOM-MIDDLE panel — ENHANCED LIGHT THEME. On a near-white page
    surface, two stacked note cards with slate text, a blue left rule and a
    faint blue tint; each card led by a muted small-caps label bar above a
    dark slate body bar; every label and bar clearly contrast AA against its
    card.

    BOTTOM-RIGHT panel — JS-OFF DEGRADED. No cards, no rules, no tint, no
    labels: four short plain rust/slate placeholder lines of prose at the
    panel's top-left, reading as ordinary unstyled authored text.

    Across all six panels the accent rule and faint tint stay quiet (never an
    opaque colour-block card), the type label is always a readable small-caps
    word, and no line of text in any panel is occluded, blurred, or dimmed
    below its label.
  negative: legible sentences, long paragraphs, digits, watermark, logo,
    light mode outside the bottom-middle panel, 3D, photorealism, faces,
    avatars, robot mascots, more than six panels, an opaque filled card, a
    solid colour-block thought, cards in the bottom-right panel, small-caps
    labels in the bottom-right panel, colour-only type coding, a solid rule
    on the unknown-type card
  style: flat dark-mode product UI illustration, squared corners, hairline
    borders, slate and violet palette (one amber warning, one light-theme
    panel), six-panel mode comparison

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1600
    height: 900
    aspect_ratio: '16:9'

attachments:
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-thought/npl-thought-render-enhanced-900.png
    role: reference
    description: enhanced render — canonical classified set, unknown type (dashed amber + "· unknown"), no-type sub-container, class-form, light theme (fixture)
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-thought/npl-thought-render-jsoff-900.png
    role: reference
    description: JS-off render — authored thoughts as plain unstyled prose, no cards or labels (fixture)
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-thought/npl-thought-fullpage-1280.png
    role: reference
    description: site reference page (source view) — chrome, attribute table, example + variant placement

requirements:
  subject: six panels of one typed thought-bubble element — enhanced canonical
    classified set, enhanced unknown-type warning, enhanced no-type
    sub-container, enhanced class-form, enhanced light theme, JS-off plain prose
  palette: slate navy background, slate panels, hairline borders, violet accent
    rule and tint, one amber warning card, one light-theme panel, near-white
    body bars, muted small-caps labels
  composition: three-by-two grid of equal panels, each thought stack at a
    consistent top-left position, identical card anatomy across the element-form
    panels
  do:
    - keep each thought a quiet ruled note card — accent rule plus faint tint,
      never an opaque block
    - keep every body bar brighter and more legible than its muted type label
    - tell the types apart by the label word, never by colour alone
    - give the unknown-type card a DASHED amber rule and an "unknown" suffix
    - give the no-type sub-container's lines no card chrome at all
  dont:
    - any legible sentence, digits, or logos (but the one-word type labels)
    - occluding, blurring, or dimming any line in any panel
    - a card, rule, tint, or generated label in the bottom-right (JS-off) panel
    - an opaque or solid accent-filled thought card
    - extra chrome (badges, counts, buttons) the tag does not define

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.7
  required_pass:
    - mode_differentiation
    - label_is_the_cue
  criteria:
    mode_differentiation:
      weight: 3
      description: The six panels are visibly distinct — canonical labelled
        stack, dashed amber unknown card, sub-container lines without chrome,
        single class-form card, light-theme stack, and a chrome-free JS-off
        panel of plain lines
      fail_signals:
        - card, rule, tint, or label present in the bottom-right panel
        - the unknown-type card's rule is solid, not dashed
        - the no-type sub-container lines carry a rule, tint, or label
        - the light-theme panel shows dark-mode cards
        - card anatomy differs between the element-form panels
    label_is_the_cue:
      weight: 3
      description: Each typed card is named by a readable small-caps type label,
        so types are told apart by their word, never by hue alone; no text is
        occluded, blurred, or dimmed below its label in any panel
      fail_signals:
        - two different types share one colour with no label word to separate them
        - missing small-caps label on a typed card
        - body bars dimmer than their labels
        - blur, redaction, or occlusion overlays on any bar
    quiet_not_opaque:
      weight: 2
      description: Every thought card is a faintly tinted, ruled note — never a
        solid opaque colour block; the accent rule stays thin
      fail_signals:
        - opaque or solid accent-filled card
        - thick or heavy accent rule
        - glossy 3D look
    theme_fidelity:
      weight: 2
      description: Dark slate + violet, squared hairline panels, flat style,
        one amber warning and one light-theme panel
      fail_signals:
        - light theme outside the one intended panel
        - rounded card corners
        - no amber warning distinction on the unknown card
  reject_if:
    - any legible sentence, digits, watermark, or logo beyond the one-word
      type labels
    - an occluded, blurred, or hidden line in any panel
    - a card, rule, tint, or generated label in the JS-off panel
    - colour-only type coding with no label word
    - more than six panels or a chaotic layout

tags:
  - semtext
  - reference
  - npl-thought